Changelog: 18-11-2026 04:15:16

Release 1.3.0.

Changelog: 18-11-2026 02:50:27

Added. The managers' new design, as PPSSPP Manager's, PCSX2 Manager's and RPCS3 Manager's: a Memory cards tab
with the saves shadPS4 keeps, each under its game's title (export to a .zip, import, delete). Clear logs, a tab
beside Log that is a button, empties the app's log file and the Log tab and removes the older log files. Start
game stands beside Your games. The six tabs share the window's whole width and are pills as the ones above them.
Play time moved from the header to the row of action pills. Under the header's pills only the links to shadPS4's
release notes and the wiki are left, in the type of a pill's caption; the introduction went. shadPS4's state is
one line. Under the games an info symbol stands in for the line of text about Steam. The window opens 900 wide
(it was 980), which is its narrowest, and 606 high (it was 800); the Settings tab scrolls when it is higher than
the window.

Changelog: 17-11-2026 14:53:56

Release 1.2.0.

Changelog: 15-11-2026 11:26:39

Release 1.1.0.

Changelog: 15-11-2026 10:16:55

Fixed. Escape and a controller's B are core's exit_keys (the app's own copy is gone): B closes the window only once
the app has had the focus for half a second, so the press that closed another app does not close this one too; a
dialog and a menu keep their own Escape. Start game is core's ActionTab: the arrow keys and Ctrl+Tab pass it by, only a click on it starts the game.

Changelog: 15-11-2026 07:43:15

Release 1.0.2.

Changelog: 15-11-2026 03:22:26

Fixed. The uninstall on a computer where the app is not installed says so ("… is not installed: nothing to remove.")
and stops, without asking for the sudo password; it listed its removal steps for what was never there (owner,
15-11-2026). With anything of the app there, it uninstalls as before.

Changelog: 14-11-2026 13:58:40

Release 1.0.1.

Changelog: 14-11-2026 12:12:03

Fixed. The tooltip and the log line about a newer shadPS4 release say "once it has been tried on the console", not "on
the board". Extract PKG's note under the destination folder no longer points to an Add folder button the app does not
have: for a folder that is not one of shadPS4's game folders it says the game will not show in the list, and names the
folders to extract into. Comments say the console instead of the board.

